REDISTRIBUTING THE IMAGE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Publishing a container image built from this repository is redistribution of
GPL-licensed software inside it, and carries obligations that this repository's
Apache-2.0 licence does not satisfy on your behalf.

There are two separate duties and satisfying one does not satisfy the other:
include a copy of the licence text, and offer the corresponding source for any
compiled object code. Per-file SPDX headers are notices, not a licence copy.

Source is present in the image, so the source duty is already met, for:
ComfyUI v0.30.2, comfyui-manager, ultralytics, plyfile, easydict,
comfyui-embedded-docs and PyGithub.

A source offer is required for, at least: bpy (Blender) 4.5.9, pymeshlab
2025.7.post1, igraph 1.0.0, pymeshfix 0.18.1, comfy-3d-viewers 0.2.44, the two
separate GPL ffmpeg builds, and the Ubuntu 22.04 base layer.

Blender specifically: the wheel DOES ship 746 Python source files, 395 of them
GPL-2.0-or-later, so the licence-copy duty applies; it ships no copy of the GPL
text itself; and the C/C++ source behind its 213MB compiled object is absent, so
the source-offer duty applies too. Its metadata declares GPL-3.0 while its shipped
files say GPL-2.0-or-later.

The image does not carry comfyui_controlnet_aux, because its CMU-licensed
folders (above) forbid distribution (the owner's decision, 2026-09-30).
scripts/entrypoint.sh fetches it from GitHub, at the commit the Dockerfile pins,
when a container starts; ASSET_ENGINE_CONTROLNET_AUX=0 skips it.

Unresolved: ultralytics is AGPL-3.0 and this image exists to serve a network
port, which engages AGPL section 13 for anyone hosting it rather than running it
locally. That was not analysed.

Note that this inventory was taken from a container built from an earlier
Dockerfile than the one in this repository. Rebuild and re-verify before relying
on it. The full inventory, with what remains unresolved, is in
docs/guide/redistributing.md.

